  "body": "Found by the worker of #2210 (PR #2214); filed by an agent.\n\nWhat happens: the UI helper `boundary_picks::extend_to_loop` reads face normals in the model frame. It does not apply the part alignment of the setup. For a turn about Z the result is the same. For a flip or a free angle, the helper can add a different face to the selection than the one that the user expects.\n\nExpected: the helper reads the normals in the setup frame, with the same transform that the generators use for picks.\n\nEffect: the helper fills in a selection only. It does not cut. The user sees the selected faces before a generate. A wrong pick is thus visible, but it can go into a boundary that the generator then obeys.\n\nEvidence: PR #2214 body, \"not exercised\"; `docs/decisions/2210-aligned-area-controls.md`.\n\nDone means: a test with a flipped setup (180 degrees about X) pins that `extend_to_loop` selects the same faces as in the same part with the flip built into its mesh.\n",
